A-06 / A-07 scoped storage, A/B on DN-ENG41 (Android 14, serial T3515NNFBC000055),
with the share-sheet half on the zxing_api36 emulator. 2026-11-02

Two APKs from the same tree, differing only in this fix.

== A-06, history CSV export ==

Setup: two rows inserted straight into the app's history database over run-as, because
the Send button only appears when the history is non-empty and this device's camera
cannot be aimed at a barcode from the command line.

  BEFORE: dialog "Sorry, the SD card is not accessible."
    W HistoryManager: Couldn't make dir /storage/emulated/0/BarcodeScanner/History

  AFTER: no dialog; the file is written and the Intent is built.
    cache/exports/history/history-1793592610913.csv, 195 bytes:
      "https://example.com/a06","https://example.com/a06","QR_CODE","1793592215000",...
      "9780140328721","9780140328721","EAN_13","1793592215000",...
    Intent: act=android.intent.action.SEND typ=text/csv flg=0x80001
            clip={text/comma-separated-values hasLabel(0) {U(content)}}
    flg 0x1 is FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION, 0x80000 is FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_DOCUMENT.

  DN-ENG41 has no app that accepts text/csv, so the send ends in a caught
  ActivityNotFoundException. On the API 36 emulator the share sheet opens and offers
  Drive and Gmail with zero permission denials, but neither has an account on that
  emulator, so a mail composer holding the attachment was never seen. The step that
  this leaves unobserved -- another app reading the bytes through the provider -- is
  the same call the A-07 case below does observe.

== A-07, share the barcode as an image ==

  BEFORE: dialog "Sorry, the SD card is not accessible."
    W EncodeActivity: Couldn't make dir /storage/emulated/0/BarcodeScanner/Barcodes

  AFTER: cache/exports/barcodes/A_07_check.png, 3114 bytes, and the share goes
  through to a real app. The system print service received it and rendered the QR in
  its print preview, which means it opened the content:// URI and read the bytes.

  The exported file pulled back off the device and decoded with this fork's :core:
    QR_CODE  A-07 check
  (the file itself, not a screenshot:
   docs/maint/reports/a07-exported-barcode-DN-ENG41-20261102.png)

== The bug this A/B found in the first version of the fix ==

The first attempt set EXTRA_STREAM and FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION and let
startActivity build the ClipData, which is what it normally does. The target app
could read the file -- the print preview above -- but the share sheet could not:

  W ContentProviderHelper: Permission Denial: opening provider
    androidx.core.content.FileProvider from ProcessRecord{com.android.intentresolver}
    that is not exported from UID 10198
  D ImagePreviewImageLoader: java.io.IOException: java.lang.SecurityException: ...

Intent.createChooser copies the target's ClipData and flags at the moment it is
built, and startActivity builds the ClipData later, so the chooser was handed none
and had no grant of its own. ExportFiles.grantRead now sets the ClipData itself.
After that, the chooser Intent carries both:

  START u0 {act=android.intent.action.CHOOSER flg=0x1
    cmp=com.android.intentresolver/.ChooserActivity
    clip={image/png hasLabel(0) {U(content)}}}

and the denial count over the same run is 0.

== Stale-export sweep ==

A file dated 2026-10-01 planted in cache/exports/barcodes was gone after the next
export, and the one written minutes earlier was kept:
  before: A_07_check.png (12:08), stale-A_07.png (2026-10-01)
  after:  A_07_again.png (12:09), A_07_check.png (12:08)
